 "poem": "Farewell, my dear boy! When haply again\nWe meet thee on that fatiguing journey,\nWhen first I saw thy face and explain\nMy love for thee by some dreary morality,\nThen might my soul repose upon again,\nThat moment of our distant farewell!\nIt were but fair to hear thy voice refrain,\nAnd kiss the hand which both thy loves compel.\nNot even in your simplest conversation, dear,\nDid I forget one word, save again\nToward this hour we parted. Wish,\nI say wish, (more than all words can explain",
